per (index, faccode) it returns that row's value or null; the \code{coalesce()}
that follows turns null into \code{fill}. The local branch uses \code{pivot_wider()},
which is clearer and errors loudly on the duplicate-key case.

Both branches emit the full \code{facility_codes} set in registry order, and both
are covered by the same tests.
